import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    /**
     * Given a positive integer n, you have to make a pile of n levels of stones.
     * The first level has n stones.
     * The number of stones in the next level is:
     *     - the next odd number if n is odd.
     *     - the next even number if n is even.
     * Return the number of stones in each level in a list, where element at index
     * i represents the number of stones in the level (i+1).
     *
     * @param n a positive integer
     * @return a list of integers representing the number of stones in each level
     */
    public List<Integer> makeAPile(int n) {
        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        result.add(n);
        int nextNumber = n + (n % 2 == 0 ? 2 : 1);
        while (n > 1) {
            n = nextNumber;
            nextNumber = n + (n % 2 == 0 ? 2 : 1);
            result.add(n);
        }
        return result;
    }
}
```

This function uses a while loop to generate the sequence of stone levels. It starts with the initial number of stones and keeps adding the next odd or even number to generate the next level. The loop continues until there is only one level left, which is the last level of stones. The result is then returned as a list.

