Here's the implementation of the `fizzBuzz` method in Java:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.lang.*;

class Solution {
    /**
    Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.
    >>> fizzBuzz(50)
    0
    >>> fizzBuzz(78)
    2
    >>> fizzBuzz(79)
    3
     */
    public int fizzBuzz(int n) {
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if ((i % 11 == 0 || i % 13 == 0) && String.valueOf(i).contains("7")) {
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Solution solution = new Solution();
        System.out.println(solution.fizzBuzz(50)); // 0
        System.out.println(solution.fizzBuzz(78)); // 2
        System.out.println(solution.fizzBuzz(79)); // 3
    }
}
```

This implementation iterates through all integers less than `n` and checks if they are divisible by 11 or 13 and contain the digit 7. If both conditions are met, the count is incremented. Finally, the method returns the count.

